Description: Enable 3D off starts flat; the told-once notices stay on screen; a state file's former format is told
 Patch 0001 makes Crystal Eyes ParaView's configured stereo type, so with Enable 3D
 off the render view gets the native (mono) widget while the type is still Crystal
 Eyes, and pqQVTKWidget asked the stereo widget, which was not made, for its stereo
 format: a null pointer and a crash at every start (Qt/Core/pqQVTKWidget.cxx, the
 request after "if active stereo requested"). The request is now made only when the
 stereo-capable widget was made.
 .
 The told-once notices (a saved setting or state file asked for a former output
 format; this desktop shows no 3D areas) were opened as dialogs of the main window.
 On Wayland Qt recreates the main window's platform window when the first
 render-to-texture widget (VTK's QVTKOpenGLNativeWidget in the color map editor) is
 added to it, and a dialog parented to the window it replaces is closed with it, so
 the notices were never seen. They now open in a box of their own
 (Qt/Core/pqStereoEditionNotice.h, private), after the view's next frame and once the
 main window is on screen, and their sentences also go to the log.
 .
 ParaView's view applies its configured stereo type when its VTK objects are made
 (vtkSMRenderViewProxy::CreateVTKObjects), which in a state load comes after the
 state's values: a state file naming Anaglyph opened in the pair without a word. A
 former output format met there is now noted on the proxy (an annotation) for
 pqRenderView::keepStereoPair to tell.
